{"name":"Rocky Shelter","hex":"#b8baba","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"rocky","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Abounding in, or full of, rocks; consisting of rocks.","Like a rock; rigid, solid."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Easily rocked; unstable.","Encountering many problems; difficult, troubled; also, in danger or distress."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rocky"},{"term":"shelter","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Somewhere one can find protection.\nA place where a person or animal may find protection from the elements (especially rain, storms, or cold) sometimes as a place to sleep (such as a cave).","A place where a person or animal may find protection from the elements (especially rain, storms, or cold) sometimes as a place to sleep (such as a cave)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To provide cover from damage or harassment; to shield; to protect.","To take cover."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shelter"}],"entries":[{"title":"Rocky","blocks":[{"text":"Rocky is a 1976 American sports drama film directed by John G. Avildsen and written by and starring Sylvester Stallone. It is the first installment in the Rocky film series and also stars Talia Shire, Burt Young, Carl Weathers, and Burgess Meredith. In the film, Rocky Balboa (Stallone), a poor small-time club fighter and loanshark debt collector from Philadelphia, gets an unlikely once in a lifetime shot at the world heavyweight championship held by Apollo Creed (Weathers)."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/1/18/Rocky_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rocky"},{"title":"Shelter","blocks":[{"text":"A shelter is an architectural structure or natural formation providing protection from the local environment. A shelter can serve as a home or be provided by a residential institution. It can be understood 